# Greenwich .gitignore. Written before the first git add, never after.
#
# The rule this file enforces: code and configuration are in the repo, data and results are
# not. An ignored file is a file that exists on one machine only, which is the fault the repo
# exists to end, so anything ignored here must have a home on the data root instead. That
# home is E:\Avia\greenwich, resolved by config.py from AVIA_LOCAL_CACHE.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
.venv/

# --- workbooks: every one of them is either an input or an output, never source ----
# Client and reference models (Plovdiv, Project East, TNGHIA, Scanner, TAS, the Space
# Facilities model) moved to E:\Avia\greenwich\reference on 8 August 2026, hash-verified.
# Client-confidential material must never enter a code repository.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.xlsb

# --- generated model output -------------------------------------------------------
# The 18 skeleton and demo workbooks built between 15 and 17 July are on the data root at
# E:\Avia\greenwich\outputs_18Jul. A build writes to config.output_dir().
chain_tmp/
outputs/

# --- charts and documents produced by a run ----------------------------------------
*.png
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.docx

# --- machine-local and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
oracle_state.json
~$*
*.tmp
.write_test*

# --- secrets: never committed --------------------------------------------------------
# Greenwich reads no credential today. The entries stand so that the first one added has
# nowhere to go by accident, per point 4 of the tool standard.
secrets.py
secrets.json
*_key.txt
*_password.txt
.env

# --- NOT ignored, deliberately, so each decision is visible --------------------------
#   selftest_fixtures/   the pinned inputs the 18 assertions run against. Small, and the
#                        suite is worthless without them. Tracked.
#   ingest_demo/         the vendor ingest demo tables. Inputs, not outputs. Tracked.
#   *.tsv                the 15 model tables, including t4_engine_pack.tsv which is empty
#                        by design and stays empty until pack2t1 exists. Tracked.
#   frontend/            forecast_studio.html, the Studio front end. Source. Tracked.
#   attic/               superseded modules, committed with a reason each. A committed
#                        attic is a record; a deletion is a loss.
